			"notes": "First release of **ChatScope** — a configurable live web dashboard for Minecraft chat (Fabric 1.21.11).\n\n## What it does\nMirrors your in-game chat, server info, and player list to a web page at http://localhost:25534, updated live over a WebSocket.\n\n## Highlights\n- **Configurable sections & filters** — split chat into as many named sections as you want using your own regex patterns, and hide noise with filters. Everything is managed from an in-browser settings panel and applies instantly.\n- **Player list & profiles** — tab-list style player list (heads, ping, game mode), Online/Offline tabs, and per-player profiles with an interactive 3D skin viewer and full logged message history (searchable, paginated).\n- **Per-server chat log** stored locally in SQLite, one table per server.\n- Minecraft colours and hover tooltips preserved, dark/light theme, accessibility mode, mention sound, live viewer count, chat search, and text export.\n\n## Install\nDrop `chatscope-1.0.0.jar` and the [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api) into your Minecraft 1.21.11 `mods` folder, launch, and open http://localhost:25534.\n\nSee the README for how to configure sections and filters."
		}
